# 3. TECHNOLOGY STACK

Use the following architecture.

## Frontend

- Angular with a currently supported stable version.
- TypeScript.
- Angular Router.
- Angular Reactive Forms.
- Angular Signals or an appropriate state-management approach.
- RxJS.
- Tailwind CSS or a consistent component-based styling system.
- Angular Material or custom reusable components.
- Chart.js or ECharts for analytics.
- PWA support for mobile installation where appropriate.

Angular 16 may be used as a migration baseline if the existing project requires it. For a new production project, prefer a currently supported Angular release.

Do not introduce React into the same application without a clear architectural reason.

## Backend

- Python.
- Django.
- Django REST Framework.
- Django ORM.
- JWT-based authentication with secure refresh-token handling.
- Django permissions and custom role-based access control.
- Celery for background tasks.
- Redis for caching and background-job coordination.

## Database

- PostgreSQL.
- Proper foreign keys and constraints.
- Database indexing.
- Transaction management.
- Migration management.
- Audit-history records.

## AI Services

- Python-based AI service.
- LLM API integration through a provider abstraction.
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) for approved institutional information.
- Speech-to-text and text-to-speech through replaceable providers.
- AI usage monitoring and cost controls.

## Infrastructure

- Docker and Docker Compose.
- Environment-based configuration.
- Nginx or an equivalent production reverse proxy.
- Managed PostgreSQL in production.
- Object storage for uploaded documents.
- CI/CD pipeline.
- Centralised application logging and monitoring.

Choose stable, compatible dependency versions. Pin dependencies and document upgrade procedures.

