# 4. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS

Implement role-based access control at both frontend and backend levels.

## 4.1 Student

Students can:

- View personal dashboard.
- View their timetable.
- View attendance.
- View assignments and deadlines.
- Submit assignments.
- Create personal study tasks.
- Track study sessions.
- Create academic and skill goals.
- View quizzes and results.
- Access approved learning resources.
- Interact with the AI learning assistant.
- View personal progress analytics.
- Receive notifications.
- Manage permitted profile information.

Students must never access another student's private academic records.

## 4.2 Faculty

Faculty can:

- View assigned classes and subjects.
- View their timetable.
- Publish assignments.
- Upload notes and learning materials.
- Create quizzes.
- Record attendance for authorised classes.
- Evaluate submissions.
- Enter and update marks within authorised workflows.
- Publish announcements.
- View class-level progress.
- Identify students who may need academic support.

Faculty must not modify academic records outside their assigned permissions.

## 4.3 Mentor

Mentors can:

- View assigned students.
- View permitted learning progress.
- Review study goals.
- Identify missed tasks and concerning progress trends.
- Record mentoring sessions.
- Create follow-up actions.
- Set review dates.
- Track intervention progress.

Mentor analytics must be supportive and explainable, not punitive.

## 4.4 HOD

HODs can:

- Manage department-level academic information.
- View department faculty and students.
- Monitor subject and section progress.
- Review attendance summaries.
- Review academic reports.
- Approve designated workflows.
- Monitor departmental performance.

## 4.5 Examination Cell

The examination team can:

- Configure examinations.
- Create examination schedules.
- Manage assessment records.
- Enter or import marks.
- Verify results.
- Publish authorised results.
- Generate examination reports.

## 4.6 Administrator

Administrators can:

- Configure institution structure.
- Manage users and roles.
- Create departments.
- Create programmes and batches.
- Manage academic years and semesters.
- Manage sections and subjects.
- Allocate faculty.
- Configure timetables.
- Manage system settings.
- View audit logs.
- Import and export approved records.

## 4.7 Accounts Role

For the later fee-management module:

- Manage fee structures.
- Generate invoices.
- Record payments.
- Issue receipts.
- Track dues.
- Generate financial reports.

Never allow one role to access another role's functionality merely because a frontend route is hidden. Enforce all permissions on the backend.

