# 7. AI LEARNING ASSISTANT

Build an AI assistant that helps students organise and understand their learning.

## 7.1 Text Assistant

Students should be able to ask:

- What should I study today?
- What assignments are pending?
- When is my next class?
- How much did I study this week?
- Which tasks are overdue?
- Explain a topic from my approved syllabus.
- Create a revision plan for my upcoming test.
- Generate practice questions from approved study material.

## 7.2 Voice Assistant

Implement:

- Microphone permission handling.
- Speech-to-text.
- Text response.
- Text-to-speech.
- Voice playback controls.
- Clear microphone recording status.
- Text alternative for every voice interaction.

Example:

Student: "What should I complete today?"

Assistant: "You have two pending assignments and one study goal. Your DAA assignment is due tomorrow. I suggest completing it first, then spending 30 minutes revising Operating Systems."

## 7.3 AI Data Grounding

The AI must retrieve relevant information from authorised sources:

- Student timetable.
- Student assignments.
- Official syllabus.
- Approved faculty notes.
- Academic calendar.
- Student goals.
- Learning resources.

Never allow AI to invent:

- Assignment deadlines.
- Attendance records.
- Examination dates.
- Marks.
- Faculty instructions.
- Official syllabus information.

If information is missing, explicitly say that it is unavailable.

## 7.4 AI Permissions and Safety

The AI assistant must never independently:

- Mark attendance.
- Change marks.
- Submit an assignment.
- Delete academic records.
- Sign documents.
- Change official timetable entries.

For any operation that changes records, require an explicit user action and normal backend permission validation.

Keep AI-generated quizzes and study plans clearly labelled. Allow faculty review where appropriate.

## 7.5 AI Cost Management

Build:

- Provider-independent AI service.
- API key management through environment secrets.
- Request logging without unnecessarily storing sensitive conversations.
- Rate limits.
- Token and usage monitoring.
- Configurable model selection.
- Daily and monthly budget limits.
- Graceful fallback when the AI service is unavailable.

Do not hardcode API keys.

