- Subject code.
- Subject name.
- Credits.
- Programme.
- Semester.
- Syllabus.
- Assigned faculty.
- Learning materials.

## 8.5 Timetable Management

Administrators and authorised faculty should be able to:

- Create timetable entries.
- Assign faculty.
- Assign subjects.
- Assign classrooms.
- Configure weekdays.
- Set class start and end times.
- Publish timetable changes.

Validate:

- Faculty time conflicts.
- Section time conflicts.
- Classroom conflicts.
- Invalid time ranges.

Students should see only the timetable applicable to their section.

## 8.6 Attendance Management

Faculty should be able to:

1. Select an authorised class.
2. Select date and period.
3. View enrolled students.
4. Mark attendance.
5. Submit attendance.
6. Correct attendance through an authorised workflow.

Attendance statuses:

- Present.
- Absent.
- Late.
- On approved leave, if institutional policy supports it.

Include:

- Subject-wise attendance.
- Overall attendance.
- Attendance percentage.
- Monthly summaries.
- Attendance correction requests.
- Faculty submission history.
- Audit history.

Never permit students to edit official attendance.

## 8.7 Assignment Management

Faculty can:

- Create assignments.
- Select subject and section.
- Add instructions.
- Attach files.
- Set issue date.
- Set deadline.
- Configure allowed submission formats.
- Publish assignments.

Students can:

- View assignments.
- Upload submissions.
- Resubmit when allowed.
- View submission status.
- Receive feedback.
- View marks after publication.

Record submission timestamps and preserve previous submissions where required.

## 8.8 Quiz and Assessment Management

Support:

- Multiple-choice questions.
- Multiple-answer questions.
- True/false.
- Short-answer questions.
- Subject-wise question banks.
- Timed quizzes.
- Configurable attempts.
- Automatic objective evaluation.
- Faculty evaluation for subjective answers.
- Result publication.

Include periodic tests, such as fortnightly or monthly assessments, when configured by faculty.

Do not allow students to access answers or results before their permitted release time.

## 8.9 Examination and Results

Include:

- Examination creation.
- Examination schedule.
- Subject mapping.
- Student eligibility.
- Marks entry.
- Marks verification.
- Result publication.
- Subject-wise results.
- Semester-wise results.
- Downloadable reports.

Changes to published marks must require an authorised correction process and must be audited.

## 8.10 Document Management and Signing

Support:

- Student document uploads.
- Faculty document uploads.
- Administrative document verification.
- Document status.
- Approval and rejection comments.
- Version history.
- Signature workflow.

For electronic signing, use a compliant digital-signature provider where legally required. Do not present a simple typed name or checkbox as a legally valid digital signature.

## 8.11 Notifications

Implement in-app notifications first.

Later integrations may include:

- Email.
- SMS.
- Push notifications.
- WhatsApp through an approved provider.

Notification examples:

- New assignment.
- Upcoming deadline.
- Timetable change.
- Attendance update.
- Quiz announcement.
- Results published.
- Mentor follow-up.
- Institutional announcement.

Allow users to configure permitted notification preferences.

## 8.12 Events and Opportunities

Provide an optional module for:

- Hackathons.
- Internships.
- Workshops.
- Coding competitions.
- Technical events.
- Placement preparation activities.

Allow authorised administrators or faculty to publish opportunities.

