# 19. DEVELOPMENT RULES

Follow these rules throughout the project.

1. Do not generate the entire application as one giant file.
2. Do not use fake frontend data as a replacement for backend integration.
3. Do not create buttons that do nothing.
4. Do not hardcode student records or dashboard values.
5. Do not bypass authentication during normal application usage.
6. Do not trust frontend permissions alone.
7. Do not expose secrets in source code.
8. Do not allow AI to modify official academic records autonomously.
9. Do not duplicate business logic across frontend and backend.
10. Do not ignore failed tests or build errors.
11. Do not silently change existing working features.
12. Do not introduce unnecessary dependencies.
13. Do not implement a feature without validation and error handling.
14. Do not claim a feature is production-ready without testing it.
15. Keep the application usable on mobile, tablet, and desktop.
16. Maintain documentation whenever architecture or APIs change.
17. Use Git commits with meaningful messages at logical milestones.
18. Ask for approval before connecting to real Vignan systems or importing real student information.
19. Record assumptions where official institutional requirements are not yet known.
20. Prefer a working, secure MVP over a large unfinished collection of modules.

