# 20. DEFINITION OF DONE

A module is complete only when:

- Frontend screens are implemented.
- Backend endpoints are implemented.
- Database models and migrations are complete.
- Permissions are enforced.
- Input validation works.
- Loading and error states are implemented.
- Unit tests pass.
- Relevant integration tests pass.
- API documentation is updated.
- Responsive behaviour is checked.
- No critical console or server errors remain.
- The feature has been tested with the appropriate role.

The application is ready for a Vignan pilot only when:

- Student, faculty, mentor, and admin workflows work.
- Academic records are permission-protected.
- Attendance and marks changes are auditable.
- The daily planner produces valid schedules.
- AI responses are grounded in approved information.
- Backup restoration has been tested.
- Security testing has been completed.
- Performance has been validated.
- Pilot users have completed user acceptance testing.
- Operational ownership and support procedures are defined.

